1
00:00:01,181 --> 00:00:09,221
The Princess Sapphire
Knight of the Ribbon

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Knight of the Ribbon,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,101 --> 00:01:50,141
Thirtieth Episode
The Phantom Kite
Flying Phantom Thief

15
00:02:17,330 --> 00:02:19,227
How delightful.

16
00:02:25,030 --> 00:02:26,460
My crown is gone!

17
00:02:26,630 --> 00:02:27,300
S-Search for it!

18
00:02:27,379 --> 00:02:28,266
Find it!

19
00:02:28,386 --> 00:02:28,813
Hurry!

20
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:41,073
The Phantom Thief Jiruba?

21
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:42,273
Yes.

22
00:02:42,885 --> 00:02:45,880
He's a strange thief who targets nothing but crowns.

23
00:02:46,599 --> 00:02:48,800
Not only has he never been caught,

24
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,340
no one has ever seen his face.

25
00:02:52,594 --> 00:02:55,227
All we know is...

26
00:02:56,726 --> 00:02:58,726
 Wait!

27
00:03:49,859 --> 00:03:53,279
He's remarkably agile and terrifyingly strong.

28
00:03:55,290 --> 00:03:57,793
Jiruba is so cool! I really admire him!

29
00:03:57,817 --> 00:03:59,153
Now see here, Sapphire...

30
00:03:59,617 --> 00:04:00,426
Okay.

31
00:04:00,790 --> 00:04:04,786
Word is that wretched Jiruba showed up in the neighboring kingdom a month ago and stole their crown—

32
00:04:05,570 --> 00:04:07,196
So that's how their crown got stolen?

33
00:04:07,220 --> 00:04:08,252
Of course it was!

34
00:04:08,276 --> 00:04:11,485
Who on earth is this Jiruba? He's a tricky thief, and no one knows where he comes from.

35
00:04:11,509 --> 00:04:15,240
Word is he won't stop stealing until he's collected a thousand crowns.

36
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,466
Jiruba's a strange one, isn't she?

37
00:04:18,449 --> 00:04:20,419
And Father... Father's in danger, too.

38
00:04:20,588 --> 00:04:22,493
Hey, don't scare me like that.

39
00:04:22,675 --> 00:04:25,260
Whatever. If they take it, just wear another one.

40
00:04:25,550 --> 00:04:26,600
That's not going to happen.

41
00:04:26,835 --> 00:04:30,720
After all, it's a treasure of Silverland, crafted by a master crown-maker.

42
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:35,705
It doesn't look any different from the other crowns.

43
00:04:35,729 --> 00:04:38,500
Still, you can never be too careful.

44
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:43,460
So if that crown is taken, we'll lose face completely before the citizens.

45
00:04:44,455 --> 00:04:47,000
I know, I know. I'll be very careful.

46
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:18,853
Wow, amazing!

47
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:20,393
So cool!

48
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:43,300
So this is the Phantom Thief Jiruba.

49
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:56,873
Someone, shoot down that chump!

50
00:06:15,943 --> 00:06:17,413
Take Sapphire's arrow!

51
00:06:39,386 --> 00:06:40,080
Hey!

52
00:06:40,126 --> 00:06:40,406
Thief!

53
00:06:40,431 --> 00:06:42,020
Give back the crown!

54
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:45,886
Tink!

55
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:46,733
Watch out!

56
00:06:53,346 --> 00:06:55,606
H-H-Help me!

57
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:56,880
Th-Thanks!

58
00:07:08,890 --> 00:07:12,300
Surely you heard the rumors from Nylon that Jiruba was coming.

59
00:07:12,466 --> 00:07:15,780
Yet you let the crown be stolen so easily! How pathetic.

60
00:07:16,030 --> 00:07:19,040
Did you forget that crown is our kingdom's treasure?

61
00:07:19,970 --> 00:07:23,413
Well, I never expected him to come from the sky!

62
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:28,700
I'll just have to wear a substitute crown for now.

63
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:34,500
Look, even if it's only temporary, the stolen original won't be coming back.

64
00:07:34,665 --> 00:07:38,006
After all, our opponent is Jiruba, and we don't even know where he is.

65
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:39,720
Alright, I just have to get it back, right?

66
00:07:39,885 --> 00:07:40,885
I'll definitely get it back.

67
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:41,968
Sapphire...

68
00:07:42,072 --> 00:07:43,320
It's all right, Mother.

69
00:07:43,735 --> 00:07:47,206
Otherwise, these two will keep speaking ill of Father.

70
00:07:49,055 --> 00:07:50,513
Impressive, Lord Sapphire.

71
00:07:50,601 --> 00:07:51,555
Still...

72
00:07:53,265 --> 00:07:56,235
how long will it take to reclaim the crown?

73
00:07:56,259 --> 00:07:59,326
We can't wait two, three, or five years...

74
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:02,160
Give me three days!

75
00:08:02,245 --> 00:08:03,245
Oh, three days?

76
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:05,400
I will definitely retrieve it within three days.

77
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:06,246
Very well then.

78
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:08,293
Indeed, that sounds wonderful, Lord Sapphire.

79
00:08:08,385 --> 00:08:09,498
I am truly impressed.

80
00:08:09,665 --> 00:08:13,700
To retrieve the crown from the Phantom Thief Jiruba in just three days... how impressive.

81
00:08:14,285 --> 00:08:17,740
Well, assuming you actually manage to get it back, that is.

82
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:21,526
This should be entertaining.

83
00:08:21,590 --> 00:08:23,300
I'll be eagerly waiting three days from now.

84
00:08:30,235 --> 00:08:33,433
What could anyone possibly do in a mere three days?

85
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:38,440
Besides, there's nothing we can do against a phantom thief flying on a kite.

86
00:08:39,125 --> 00:08:40,720
That's why I'm going to fly, too.

87
00:08:40,990 --> 00:08:41,990
W-What?

88
00:08:42,065 --> 00:08:43,159
You're going to fly?

89
00:08:43,679 --> 00:08:44,680
Yeah, with this.

90
00:08:44,855 --> 00:08:47,680
Ah, a poster for the circus in town.

91
00:08:48,239 --> 00:08:51,920
Right. I'll go there and learn acrobatics from this boy, Trott.

92
00:08:52,239 --> 00:08:53,800
Y-You can't be serious!

93
00:08:53,925 --> 00:08:56,726
For a noble prince to do circus tricks...

94
00:08:57,549 --> 00:09:00,620
Well, Dr. Uranari, do you have another way to fly?

95
00:09:00,870 --> 00:09:06,006
Oh, well, about that... No, I'll study the grand ceremony now—

96
00:09:06,030 --> 00:09:08,260
No, no, there's no time!

97
00:09:09,415 --> 00:09:10,700
The promise was for three days.

98
00:09:11,780 --> 00:09:14,200
Alright. I guess I have no choice.

99
00:09:14,460 --> 00:09:15,260
Thank goodness.

100
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:19,000
Word is this kid Trott is going to ride an kite, too.

101
00:09:19,910 --> 00:09:24,833
Dr. Uranari, find out what young Trott was doing when the crown was stolen.

102
00:09:26,111 --> 00:09:27,260
Quite the detective.

103
00:09:27,715 --> 00:09:30,360
Jiruba's true identity might be young Trott.

104
00:09:31,346 --> 00:09:32,333
I see.

105
00:09:32,819 --> 00:09:36,080
And one more thing: we have to lure out Phantom Thief Jiruba.

106
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:37,380
Lure them out?

107
00:09:37,510 --> 00:09:39,286
Yeah, well, you see...

108
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:42,140
Hmm, I see. That's good.

109
00:09:42,495 --> 00:09:44,613
Post that notice all over town, Doctor.

110
00:09:44,740 --> 00:09:47,660
Well, with this, even the Phantom Thief Jiruba is sure to take the bait. Huh?

111
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:58,200
What's this?

112
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:00,960
They're holding another military review in two nights?

113
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:01,340
Huh?

114
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:03,040
At night?

115
00:10:03,929 --> 00:10:06,839
Furthermore, the crown stolen during the recent military review was a fake

116
00:10:06,863 --> 00:10:09,800
made to fool the Phantom Thief Jiruba.

117
00:10:10,285 --> 00:10:15,280
See? There's no way the King would let a simple thief take the royal crown so easily.

118
00:10:23,019 --> 00:10:24,019
So it was a fake.

119
00:10:24,973 --> 00:10:26,480
Trott, are you ready?

120
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:29,620
You're up next. Get ready.

121
00:10:29,725 --> 00:10:30,725
Okay, got it.

122
00:10:40,779 --> 00:10:41,779
Lord Sapphire.

123
00:10:42,039 --> 00:10:43,220
Dr. Uranari, how did it go?

124
00:10:43,708 --> 00:10:47,144
It seems Trott was performing for the audience

125
00:10:47,168 --> 00:10:49,584
when the crown was stolen. Several merchants saw him.

126
00:10:49,608 --> 00:10:50,847
I see.

127
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:52,053
So it wasn't Jiruba after all.

128
00:10:52,519 --> 00:10:54,780
And notice about the crown has been posted all over town.

129
00:10:55,620 --> 00:10:56,620
Yeah, thanks.

130
00:10:56,959 --> 00:11:00,453
Then I'm off to the circus to learn kite riding, Doctor!

131
00:11:00,839 --> 00:11:02,100
Damn that Jiruba... did you see that just now?

132
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:06,000
Oh, Lord Sapphire, where are you off to?

133
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:09,200
Just a little over two days left, isn't it?

134
00:11:37,449 --> 00:11:41,160
Step right up! The master of kite riding, the famous Trott!

135
00:11:41,639 --> 00:11:44,260
To start off, "Big Wave, Small Wave!"

136
00:11:52,169 --> 00:11:54,863
Next up, "The Whirlwind Spin!"

137
00:12:12,049 --> 00:12:17,240
Next, he will paint a picture in the blue sky for you all!

138
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:42,626
Incredible! He doesn't even seem human!

139
00:12:45,990 --> 00:12:46,740
Is it you?

140
00:12:46,845 --> 00:12:48,800
The one who wants to practice kite riding?

141
00:12:49,406 --> 00:12:49,959
Yes, please!

142
00:12:50,365 --> 00:12:51,500
Please make me your apprentice.

143
00:12:52,014 --> 00:12:53,260
He wasn't surprised to see me.

144
00:12:53,815 --> 00:12:55,500
So Trott really wasn't Jiruba after all.

145
00:12:55,719 --> 00:12:58,759
You say you want to be my apprentice, but it's nothing like riding a horse, kid.

146
00:12:59,605 --> 00:13:03,313
We need someone brave, agile, and quick-witted.

147
00:13:04,189 --> 00:13:05,360
I can do that!

148
00:13:05,775 --> 00:13:08,940
I'm brave, agile, and very quick-witted.

149
00:13:09,399 --> 00:13:12,093
If I say so, it must be true.

150
00:13:12,239 --> 00:13:14,000
Sure, I'll take you as an apprentice... but what's with these soft white hands?

151
00:13:14,155 --> 00:13:16,280
They're pale and slender, just like a girl's.

152
00:13:17,055 --> 00:13:19,240
Stunt riding takes strong arms.

153
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:21,260
How rude!

154
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:22,920
They may be thin, but I'm strong!

155
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:24,560
Alright, then.

156
00:13:24,915 --> 00:13:26,880
Come over here and I'll test you.

157
00:13:33,420 --> 00:13:34,900
First, try riding this.

158
00:13:36,839 --> 00:13:38,480
Isn't that Prince Sapphire?

159
00:13:39,335 --> 00:13:41,366
What is he doing in a place like this?

160
00:13:42,205 --> 00:13:42,906
Don't tell me...

161
00:13:55,399 --> 00:13:56,399
Well, can you do it?

162
00:13:56,700 --> 00:13:57,700
I'll give it a try.

163
00:14:13,289 --> 00:14:14,493
How's that?

164
00:14:15,575 --> 00:14:16,575
Not bad.

165
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:18,113
Next is that one over there.

166
00:14:37,999 --> 00:14:38,999
Go on, give it a try.

167
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,360
Me?

168
00:14:40,620 --> 00:14:41,300
That's right.

169
00:14:50,596 --> 00:14:51,396
No good.

170
00:14:51,420 --> 00:14:52,420
Relax your body.

171
00:14:52,580 --> 00:14:54,019
The boss is calling for you.

172
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:54,666
Coming!

173
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:57,180
I'll be right back, so keep practicing until I return.

174
00:15:01,429 --> 00:15:02,880
Time for a quick break while he's gone.

175
00:15:06,225 --> 00:15:08,639
Who is it? Scoundrel, show yourself!

176
00:15:12,865 --> 00:15:13,819
Show yourself!

177
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:21,060
Sorry to keep you waiting.

178
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:23,620
That won't do. You need to practice.

179
00:15:24,379 --> 00:15:25,740
Have you gotten any better?

180
00:15:26,325 --> 00:15:27,446
Practice? I've got bigger problems!

181
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:29,493
I was almost killed!

182
00:15:29,780 --> 00:15:32,366
Out of nowhere, someone threw knives at me!

183
00:15:34,326 --> 00:15:35,240
What's so funny?

184
00:15:35,575 --> 00:15:39,086
If you can't dodge a knife or two, how do you expect to ride a kite?

185
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:41,180
Didn't some flying swords come at you?

186
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:43,680
Yeah, that's them! That's the ones!

187
00:15:44,575 --> 00:15:46,340
My hand slipped.

188
00:15:47,245 --> 00:15:49,586
Why don't you switch to a bigger target?

189
00:15:52,109 --> 00:15:53,700
If something like this falls on me, I'll be squashed flat!

190
00:15:54,045 --> 00:15:55,060
There we go.

191
00:15:58,800 --> 00:15:59,800
Alright, that's enough.

192
00:16:00,529 --> 00:16:02,833
More importantly, why do you want to learn kite-riding?

193
00:16:03,715 --> 00:16:06,900
I have my reasons. I must master it by tomorrow night, no matter what.

194
00:16:08,260 --> 00:16:08,640
I see.

195
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:09,940
Alright, got it.

196
00:16:10,495 --> 00:16:12,020
I'll make sure you learn.

197
00:16:12,375 --> 00:16:16,120
The key to kite-riding is arm strength and leg movement for balance.

198
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:21,620
Your left arm is too weak.

199
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:23,393
Come on, get up.

200
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:24,760
Get up and try again.

201
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:28,926
Remember, keep equal strength in both arms.

202
00:16:29,669 --> 00:16:31,706
If you lose that, you'll lose your balance and fall.

203
00:16:33,469 --> 00:16:35,440
At this rate, you won't be able to ride the kite by tomorrow.

204
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:42,800
No, no.

205
00:16:42,910 --> 00:16:43,910
Keep trying!

206
00:16:44,045 --> 00:16:44,498
Come on!

207
00:16:55,209 --> 00:16:56,993
I've finally learned to ride the kite!

208
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:00,060
Just you wait.

209
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:01,460
Damn you, Phantom Thief Jiruba.

210
00:17:03,959 --> 00:17:05,359
What an incredible fellow.

211
00:17:05,784 --> 00:17:07,440
To master it in just a single day...

212
00:17:08,899 --> 00:17:11,500
Trott, who do you think that is?

213
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:12,500
Who?

214
00:17:13,009 --> 00:17:15,153
That's Prince Sapphire of this kingdom.

215
00:17:15,974 --> 00:17:17,020
What did you say, Brother?

216
00:17:17,460 --> 00:17:18,273
Is that true?

217
00:17:18,460 --> 00:17:19,460
Yeah, it's true.

218
00:17:19,954 --> 00:17:22,220
He was there when I went to steal the crown the day before yesterday.

219
00:17:23,609 --> 00:17:25,511
No one from any kingdom suspected

220
00:17:25,535 --> 00:17:27,920
that the two of us were taking turns playing Jiruba.

221
00:17:29,319 --> 00:17:31,040
But we can't let our guard down around him.

222
00:17:31,554 --> 00:17:33,091
They're using a fake crown,

223
00:17:33,508 --> 00:17:35,480
and they've even announced the date for the coronation.

224
00:17:36,679 --> 00:17:40,266
Man, it's like he's just making fun of us.

225
00:17:40,989 --> 00:17:44,840
Alright! Tonight, I'm definitely stealing Silverland's crown.

226
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:46,293
Very well.

227
00:17:46,554 --> 00:17:48,020
So it's master against pupil.

228
00:17:53,429 --> 00:17:55,353
Sapphire, go back to the castle and wait.

229
00:17:56,319 --> 00:17:58,693
Trott!

230
00:18:03,419 --> 00:18:04,560
Look, it's Jiruba!

231
00:18:08,839 --> 00:18:10,620
Ah, that's Sapphire!

232
00:18:29,304 --> 00:18:31,779
She's safe, she's safe!

233
00:18:31,975 --> 00:18:33,506
Sapphire, are you okay?

234
00:18:33,869 --> 00:18:35,020
Yeah, I'm fine.

235
00:18:35,669 --> 00:18:39,120
Your Highness, our promised time is running short.

236
00:18:39,504 --> 00:18:40,504
I know.

237
00:18:40,698 --> 00:18:43,220
Hey, Sapphire, there's something on your back.

238
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:45,520
It's a note.

239
00:18:45,705 --> 00:18:46,320
Read it!

240
00:18:46,584 --> 00:18:49,480
<i>How dare you give me a fake crown.</i>

241
00:18:50,064 --> 00:18:52,460
<i>Tonight, I will definitely come for the real one.</i>

242
00:18:52,725 --> 00:18:53,460
<i>Phantom Thief Jiruba.</i>

243
00:18:53,645 --> 00:18:54,645
It's from Jiruba!

244
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:55,780
It's from Jiruba!

245
00:18:55,834 --> 00:18:58,900
You fell right into my trap! Sapphire challenges you to a duel!

246
00:19:08,319 --> 00:19:10,460
It's finally time for the military parade.

247
00:19:10,594 --> 00:19:13,346
Isn't there any way to stop Jiruba the Phantom Thief from coming from the sky?

248
00:19:17,753 --> 00:19:18,446
That's right.

249
00:19:18,619 --> 00:19:19,940
Flying in the sky is easy.

250
00:19:20,254 --> 00:19:22,526
We just need to pack this smoke into bags.

251
00:19:23,509 --> 00:19:25,760
Come on, Tink, make them right away!

252
00:19:32,999 --> 00:19:35,166
We'll get the crown back.

253
00:19:56,789 --> 00:19:58,260
They're drawing close!

254
00:20:03,854 --> 00:20:04,940
Something strange is falling!

255
00:20:05,759 --> 00:20:07,593
I don't know what it is, but don't let your guard down!

256
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:19,120
Quiet down!

257
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:20,160
The enemy is in the sky!

258
00:20:20,374 --> 00:20:21,700
Keep your eyes on the sky!

259
00:20:26,289 --> 00:20:27,860
Consider it stolen!

260
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:30,720
Over there!

261
00:20:30,840 --> 00:20:31,840
Damn you, Jiruba!

262
00:20:38,396 --> 00:20:39,056
Damn it!

263
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:40,080
Luminous paint!

264
00:20:40,760 --> 00:20:41,080
Jiruba!

265
00:20:41,180 --> 00:20:42,180
Prepare yourself!

266
00:20:53,789 --> 00:20:55,260
If you lose your balance, you'll fall!

267
00:20:55,414 --> 00:20:56,553
Watch out, Sapphire!

268
00:20:57,250 --> 00:20:59,506
Wh-Why do you know my name?

269
00:21:03,101 --> 00:21:04,101
Damn it!

270
00:21:05,169 --> 00:21:06,500
That crown is a fake!

271
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:07,293
What?

272
00:21:07,959 --> 00:21:09,980
I used it to catch you!

273
00:21:20,319 --> 00:21:21,440
You've beaten me!

274
00:21:40,629 --> 00:21:41,813
Y-You're Trott!

275
00:21:43,566 --> 00:21:44,186
Sapphire!

276
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:45,360
Splendid!

277
00:21:45,544 --> 00:21:46,544
I lose!

278
00:21:46,685 --> 00:21:47,513
Do whatever you want with me!

279
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:48,020
There!

280
00:21:48,044 --> 00:21:50,426
Wh-Why... Why would you do a thing like this?!

281
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:52,500
Sapphire!

282
00:21:52,639 --> 00:21:54,240
I'll tell you Jiruba's true identity!

283
00:21:54,394 --> 00:21:56,493
T-Trott has appeared again!

284
00:21:57,034 --> 00:21:58,034
Brother, stop!

285
00:21:58,160 --> 00:21:59,160
We've lost!

286
00:21:59,395 --> 00:22:00,395
Did you say "brother"?

287
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:01,700
That's right!

288
00:22:02,099 --> 00:22:03,480
We're twin brothers!

289
00:22:04,289 --> 00:22:06,720
One played Jiruba, while the other set up our alibi!

290
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:11,466
So there!

291
00:22:11,519 --> 00:22:13,046
Dr. Uranari's great invention!

292
00:22:13,279 --> 00:22:17,546
A smoke-filled flying basket to catch Phantom Thief Jiruba!

293
00:22:17,869 --> 00:22:19,966
Caught him! Caught him!

294
00:22:20,420 --> 00:22:20,740
What?!

295
00:22:20,760 --> 00:22:21,760
Damn it!

296
00:22:22,700 --> 00:22:23,393
Brother!

297
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:24,600
Give up gracefully!

298
00:22:24,914 --> 00:22:26,366
They're out of our league!

299
00:22:29,615 --> 00:22:30,821
Whoa!

300
00:22:30,894 --> 00:22:32,879
Sapphire caught Jiruba!

301
00:22:32,959 --> 00:22:34,140
Well done, well done!

302
00:22:43,969 --> 00:22:44,896
Here you are, Father!

303
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:45,920
It's the real crown!

304
00:22:47,820 --> 00:22:48,306
I beg you!

305
00:22:48,539 --> 00:22:51,160
Do whatever you want with me, just please spare my brother!

306
00:22:52,060 --> 00:22:53,060
What are you saying, Brother?!

307
00:22:53,469 --> 00:22:54,540
I'll take whatever punishment!

308
00:22:54,725 --> 00:22:55,725
Please spare my brother!

309
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:57,119
Silence!

310
00:22:57,144 --> 00:22:58,420
I won't spare either of you!

311
00:23:01,159 --> 00:23:03,980
Why were you only after the crown?

312
00:23:04,184 --> 00:23:05,300
Is there a reason for this?

313
00:23:06,762 --> 00:23:07,321
Long ago,

314
00:23:08,051 --> 00:23:10,700
our father served the king of a distant land.

315
00:23:11,424 --> 00:23:13,320
One day, when we were five...

316
00:23:19,539 --> 00:23:24,640
He accidentally scratched the crown and was sentenced to death.

317
00:23:28,569 --> 00:23:30,347
I don't care how valuable that crown is—

318
00:23:30,705 --> 00:23:32,980
which is more important, it or a human life?

319
00:23:33,799 --> 00:23:37,120
Our father, the most important person in the world to us...

320
00:23:37,557 --> 00:23:38,627
I see...

321
00:23:42,971 --> 00:23:45,826
Envoys from various nations have come demanding we hand over Jiruba.

322
00:23:46,119 --> 00:23:47,200
I'm the one who caught him!

323
00:23:47,594 --> 00:23:48,640
I'll be the judge!

324
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:54,033
He escaped!

325
00:23:54,259 --> 00:23:56,386
Phantom Thief Jiruba escaped!

326
00:23:56,420 --> 00:23:57,080
Sapphire!

327
00:23:57,399 --> 00:23:59,493
Phantom Thief Jiruba escaped!

328
00:23:59,518 --> 00:24:01,571
Catch him!

329
00:24:06,359 --> 00:24:08,927
Even the most magnificent, expensive crown is worthless

330
00:24:08,951 --> 00:24:11,960
compared to a human life.

331
00:24:14,094 --> 00:24:17,680
I think I understand why Jiruba stole every single crown.

332
00:24:17,705 --> 00:24:21,746
And I think I understand why Sapphire forgave him.

